[3.7637, "o", "\u001b[2;1H\u001b[1m══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\r\n  Kueue Preemption Demo: Priority Scheduling on GPU Fleet   \u001b[5;82H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[3.763759, "o", "\u001b[4;1H\u001b[1m══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\u001b[6;1H\u001b(B\u001b[m  This demo shows three levels of GPU workload priority:\r\n  \u001b[35m1.\u001b[39m Low-priority experiments fill available GPU capacity\u001b[5;82H\u001b[8;1H  \u001b[36m2.\u001b[39m Inference HPA scales up under load, evicting experiments\r\n  \u001b[31m3.\u001b[39m Critical pre-training job preempts even inference servers\u001b[11;1H  \u001b[2mClusters: us-east1 (8 GPUs) + us-west3 (8 GPUs) = 16 GPUs total\u001b[5;82H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
[3.763797, "o", "\u001b[14;1H\u001b[36m▸ Initial GPU state\u001b[5;82H\u001b(B\u001b[m"]
